# Active control — optional capability

Do not treat active control as required for the passive MVP unless the committed product profile says so.

Use `docs/implementation/agent_reference_index.md`; current owners are `docs/architecture/active-control.md`, `docs/contracts/operations/propagation-safeguard.md`, `docs/contracts/operations/execution-gate-control.md`, `docs/authority/high-consequence-authority.md`, and `docs/contracts/evidence-time-causality/exposure-readiness-control-proof.md`, with Implementation 010 at `docs/implementation/010_active_control_enterprise_control_plane/README.md`.

Preserve directly:

- Execution Gate ≠ Execution History ≠ Propagation Safeguard;
- readiness ≠ Gate decision ≠ issuance ≠ delivery/acceptance ≠ enforcement ≠ actual execution/non-execution;
- HOLD ≠ failed run; ADMIT ≠ actual run;
- override/fallback do not rewrite prerequisite evidence/readiness;
- Safeguard proposal/configuration/authorization/request/attempt/effective enforcement/prevention/release/recovery are distinct;
- active safeguard + non-exposure does not automatically prove prevented exposure;
- REF-028 prevention requires exact opportunity, enforcement, alternate-path coverage, and relevant protected-state/path/cohort evidence;
- release ≠ recovery;
- authorization freshness is revalidated at enforcement time as required;
- control channels require authenticity/replay protection;
- model/vector/search output cannot issue authoritative control decisions;
- SC-06 control capacity/failure domains are isolated from optional heavy workloads to the committed deployment requirement.
